course: dictionary
lesson: 8580
title: Schoolboy: two words in one
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from two smaller words joined together. Schoolboy is school plus boy, so it means a boy who goes to school. Looking at the parts is a quick way to guess what a word means.
explain: «Ryan moans about homework, so his teacher shows him a story from Sumer, about 4,000 years old, where a schoolboy gets punished for messy work and his dad has to sweeten the teacher.» The story is about school, and the schoolboy is the boy in it who gets into trouble, so a schoolboy is a boy who goes to school.
explain: Schoolboy can also come before another noun, as in «a schoolboy joke» or «a schoolboy error». Here it describes the kind of thing a schoolboy would do, often something silly or basic. Test it: a joke made by a boy who goes to school is not the same as a joke that is silly and simple, so the meaning is the second one.
fact: A schoolboy is a boy who goes to school.
fact: «Schoolboy» can be a noun, as in «a schoolboy», or come before a noun, as in «a schoolboy joke».
fact: «A schoolboy error» means a very basic mistake that even a beginner should avoid.
fact: «Schoolboy humour» means rude or silly jokes.
fact: The girl's word is «schoolgirl»; a neutral word for either is «pupil» or «student».
exercise: In Ryan's story, «a schoolboy gets punished for messy work». What is a schoolboy? | A type of school desk | A teacher in a big school | *A boy who goes to school | A grown man who works in Sumer
exercise: Mia says, «That spelling was a schoolboy error!» What does schoolboy error mean? | *A very basic mistake that even a beginner should avoid | A mistake made by a teacher on purpose | A clever trick used in class | A word from an old book
exercise: Which word is a neutral word for a pupil? | Schoolgirl | Sweeten | Schoolboy | *Student
test: Schoolboy is made of two smaller words joined together. What are they? | school and ball | school and bag | scoot and boy | *school and boy
test: What does «schoolboy humour» mean? | Very clever puns | Quiet, sad stories | Jokes told by teachers | *Rude or silly jokes
exam: Which phrase uses schoolboy before another noun to mean the kind of thing a schoolboy would do? | the schoolboy ran home | the schoolboy's bag was heavy | *a schoolboy joke | two schoolboys sang
